:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379067} :answer-field/id #uuid "644ea586-1c68-5984-87e4-3e227b404606" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02b61f1a-304a-52ec-bd4d-1f82fbd64229" :question/math-academy-id "q-177358" :question/problem "$20$ is less than $10$ **or** $4$ divides $18.$\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $S:20\\text{ is less than }10$\n\n- $R:4\\text{ divides }18$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{20\\text{ is less than }10}_{S}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }18}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∨R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03ba3c0d-f272-582d-8d60-942574bd0b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379072} {:answer/id #uuid "42a77555-4f36-5e8f-9501-c804fbbbc69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379073} {:answer/id #uuid "62c29c52-1ad1-571f-83d6-a18aa74a7f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379074} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ebdfec-e78f-531e-af1c-5f5cb9f81c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∧R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379075} {:answer/id #uuid "aaec3ae8-95ea-53ae-b2d9-ca11b71dfdff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03ba3c0d-f272-582d-8d60-942574bd0b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379072} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4bb599f-3f92-588d-be1e-d7ac21182c11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbda1364-d6b0-5d27-8b02-4a483ed9d5f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177455" :question/problem "$\\pi $ is irrational, **and** $4$ divides $10$ **or** $16.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\pi \\text{ is irrational}$\n\n- $Q:4\\text{ divides }10$\n\n- $R:4\\text{ divides }16$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\pi $ is irrational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $4$ divide to $10$ or $16.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }10}_{Q}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }16}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\pi \\text{ is irrational}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{4\\text{ divides }10\\text{ or }16}_{Q\\,∨\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧(Q∨R).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "596971f1-f6c4-5f08-a9e3-2c3d69f7999b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧(C∧D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379079} {:answer/id #uuid "60371bd1-6da1-59eb-9946-75529fa58c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∧(C∨D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379080} {:answer/id #uuid "13eca1b9-6e1c-5eb1-9315-4e60fefd7438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∧(C∧D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379081} {:answer/id #uuid "75779276-c6a3-52ad-a05e-783361ade704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧(C∨D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379082} {:answer/id #uuid "0f9c449a-2df6-51cd-a5b9-4e48c820d58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∨(C∨D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75779276-c6a3-52ad-a05e-783361ade704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧(C∨D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379082} :answer-field/id #uuid "11a79f10-98ff-58cf-87f3-2779d26748b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "875acf59-287e-5a2a-a577-d8e4b99c8f8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-177513" :question/problem "$10$ is composite **or** even, **and** $8$ is divisible by $2$ **or** $6.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A:10\\text{ is composite}$\n\n- $B:10\\text{ is even}$\n\n- $C:8\\text{ is divisible by }2$\n\n- $D:8\\text{ is divisible by }6$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $10$ is composite or even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{10\\text{ is composite}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{10\\text{ is even }}_{B}\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $8$ is divisible by $2$ or $6.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{8\\text{ is divisible by 2}}_{C}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{8\\text{ is divisible by }6}_{D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $C∨D.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{10\\text{ is composite }\\text{or}\\text{ even}}_{A\\,∨\\,B}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{8\\text{ is divisible by }2\\text{ or }6}_{C\\,∨\\,D},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∨B)∧(C∨D).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7b64364-9c60-5a4f-b6bd-5eaa21db1af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379086} {:answer/id #uuid "990cd40f-4545-5840-98b4-3a48edcabf70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7b64364-9c60-5a4f-b6bd-5eaa21db1af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379086} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace6cf84-38dd-5340-b072-0069ac04c826" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4db1a0e-a7cf-5c86-8976-996bb66e27d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379089} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4911ad-cee4-5661-81e8-2498f9e5f576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4db1a0e-a7cf-5c86-8976-996bb66e27d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379089} :answer-field/id #uuid "3296e062-c177-560d-a10e-7f12c5bfd741" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27bcac07-76da-5b10-ab54-bafb94735ad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379092} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2b3950-4636-5bec-a3f2-b18e14b0cbaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27bcac07-76da-5b10-ab54-bafb94735ad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379092} :answer-field/id #uuid "c51d6b8e-b82e-5199-a753-0909daa00866" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bcb77aa-4135-5a99-a34c-9bd9939f1bbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-178154" :question/problem "$$\n\\underbrace{6\\,|\\,9}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{\\overbrace{\\sqrt{3}\\in R}^{Q}\\,\\overbrace{\\text{and}}^{∧}\\,\\overbrace{15\\text{ is prime}}^{R}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∧R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∧R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∧R$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∧R) & ≡\\text{false}∧\\overbrace{(\\text{true}∧\\text{false})}^{\\text{false}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∧\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc01833-d184-501a-9036-77368e7e1d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379096} {:answer/id #uuid "99b6148a-721b-5423-80f7-ee44eb56693a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc01833-d184-501a-9036-77368e7e1d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379096} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a665940-e204-54ce-b68d-6be8e61dc083" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379095} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49099298-6210-507a-a977-dada2a0f6494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379099} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b7d77a-e7ba-512f-a50b-73d058d6e34a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49099298-6210-507a-a977-dada2a0f6494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379099} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d2c68e8-c6ba-5286-97c5-99486c87b6da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f56b3063-1cbb-581e-a72a-ef39d2f3cbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379102} {:answer/id #uuid "c5b4b748-8b7f-532b-b9cb-b72533c28f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f56b3063-1cbb-581e-a72a-ef39d2f3cbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379102} :answer-field/id #uuid "58d0b83f-00f8-59a3-8829-f2d582b29445" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b82f32e2-e84f-5a70-a3a6-715fec123e2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-178164" :question/problem "$$\n\\underbrace{3\\,|\\,16}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{\\overbrace{2.3\\in Z}^{Q}\\,\\overbrace{\\text{or}}^{∨}\\,\\overbrace{21\\text{ is prime}}^{R}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∨(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{false}∨\\overbrace{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}^{\\text{false}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c91fb2b-5607-555d-b897-f0e76765dfa6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Lower Triangular Matrix Given the Elementary Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f515a37-0532-5379-b6c5-60cae121cd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379388} {:answer/id #uuid "0f26d137-daef-5ba0-b02f-8ef0beb9e1f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379389} {:answer/id #uuid "1c8445fa-f6b7-5338-b384-7962fded25ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379390} {:answer/id #uuid "88a45256-4352-5161-b66d-e81037757768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379391} {:answer/id #uuid "1acc907a-8f9c-5345-b778-5b939debd5f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88a45256-4352-5161-b66d-e81037757768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379391} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebcf7832-5de6-5a02-b8c1-346ae0bc9869" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a83c5862-ce81-57be-a501-0eb1330527bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-32681" :question/problem "Suppose that a $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ is reduced to row echelon form using the following elementary row operations, applied in the order in which they appear:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nGiven that $C$ has the LU factorization $C=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1}$ and then ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ is equivalent to multiplying $C$ from the left by the following elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{E}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{E}_{1}}\\cdot C=U\n$$\n\nNow, since ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}C=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{2}$ and ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}C & =U \\\\ {E}_{1}C & ={E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ C & ={E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ C & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ C & =(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix})U \\\\ C & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{L}\\cdot U\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bbc9cee-6d9f-53b6-a3f9-35050e0dd0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471383} {:answer/id #uuid "4f002261-81ab-55ff-af9f-9a2b2a621724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f002261-81ab-55ff-af9f-9a2b2a621724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471384} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a28f8d-5383-5eca-ab07-4ecdbad60269" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26c62176-2c72-5180-a83a-f3021cb5c0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471385} {:answer/id #uuid "059fa7d6-c973-5f8c-b14c-0bf94b31437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "059fa7d6-c973-5f8c-b14c-0bf94b31437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471386} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d943dfd-579b-532f-b5c1-a67bf7f7b2f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b0de36-67f4-5fbd-bc5c-7e6fbd2cc1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471387} {:answer/id #uuid "899f8325-7fc0-5e7f-aed3-fc93ba710d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b0de36-67f4-5fbd-bc5c-7e6fbd2cc1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471387} :answer-field/id #uuid "f68de2b5-cce3-546e-85e3-13db4ede6900" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec98e74e-e68c-5045-a599-d3ec1260eaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-330299" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n- **I.** ${x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- **II.** $-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n- **III.** $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=1\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option II is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2a88b9c-22ee-5b00-af09-d1cdae976ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471389} {:answer/id #uuid "699c223a-b0f1-5ab1-9742-cc8cc24e7610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2a88b9c-22ee-5b00-af09-d1cdae976ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471389} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe7b73e-c8d1-5806-97dd-83443a307c30" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f77fbd2-8e41-54f7-8dab-495bfe9057db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471391} {:answer/id #uuid "b928d8c6-5415-580d-a8fc-bfe309b7a281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f77fbd2-8e41-54f7-8dab-495bfe9057db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471391} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc36a6ef-b56b-5871-97f4-e7173861f357" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5134166f-f275-568c-8bbb-42b5f7da138d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471393} {:answer/id #uuid "37b63443-245b-500c-9c9b-3ed20a0c4b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b63443-245b-500c-9c9b-3ed20a0c4b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471394} :answer-field/id #uuid "07370987-e91d-5a14-9c0b-88a34bdf1ab6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "028e3468-5c29-5e67-a28b-97b2d534ac0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-330306" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n- **I.** ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$\n- **II.** $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$\n- **III.** $-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $-1$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option III is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124530 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "634729e9-7633-52d8-99fa-b00fc9cbe96a" :knowledge-point/title "Raising a Matrix to a Large Power Using the Properties of Diagonalization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85014fe6-15e2-5564-bffa-ad90af465709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-29 & 48 \\\\ -20 & 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379805} {:answer/id #uuid "4c043ac2-85b1-59df-a20c-59478e1a4e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379806} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a42728-eef7-5a58-9f94-3c8639fc3ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}19 & 24 \\\\ -20 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379807} {:answer/id #uuid "b5879874-53fc-5093-aa06-673de0a62779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & -29 \\\\ 11 & -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379808} {:answer/id #uuid "65fa80e9-ff42-5610-849e-719df033e7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 3 \\\\ 32 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85014fe6-15e2-5564-bffa-ad90af465709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-29 & 48 \\\\ -20 & 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379805} :answer-field/id #uuid "de8ad135-a11b-5489-a19a-f9ef7b2d98a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "231a6159-8f35-5b7b-8f85-d4021873942f" :question/math-academy-id "q-37628" :question/problem "Find ${M}^{32},$ where\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[32]{3}\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have been given the following diagonalization of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{P}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[32]{3}\\end{bmatrix}}_{D}\\underbrace{{\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $M=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${M}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{M}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{32} & =P{D}^{32}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[32]{3}\\end{bmatrix}}^{32}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{1}^{32} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[32]{3})^{32}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-29 & 48 \\\\ -20 & 33\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ed5119c-5ce8-52dc-bd57-f9439ea199e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a QR Factorization of a Matrix Given a Matrix With Orthogonal Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c396ef-aa94-5fde-91e0-260c09178b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380320} {:answer/id #uuid "4c5017ed-934c-561b-b1a1-2049ddab8c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380321} {:answer/id #uuid "87b3f482-5de0-50ca-b081-5eb25a4c9360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380322} {:answer/id #uuid "c60e3738-5a9e-5b51-bb8b-21ac87f694a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380323} {:answer/id #uuid "958ede67-2778-5ce8-a57e-f1838011f997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c5017ed-934c-561b-b1a1-2049ddab8c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380321} :answer-field/id #uuid "379ef46e-ea0e-5853-8ba7-b593f74e67fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "999c22e3-00be-5df4-8adf-f0fdfad70b35" :question/math-academy-id "q-95942" :question/problem "$$\n\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{bmatrix}}^{Q}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}}^{R}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ of $A$ are orthogonal, and that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained by normalizing the columns of $A,$ what is the value of ${q}_{32}\\cdot {r}_{11}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the columns of $A$ are already orthogonal, to construct an orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we simply normalize ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{‖{a}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{‖{a}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}^{Q}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{R}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{32}\\cdot {r}_{11}=-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7716a75-0eea-5e7d-8387-1aa17c566b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380575} {:answer/id #uuid "c669296d-1bdf-527a-aa02-77c5f5fc6df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380576} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbdf937-1217-53c1-8187-c84c2557e123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380577} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7651c9-51f8-5028-9d93-a70283285549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380578} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bd6a53-d027-5e1c-b16c-738508b17ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c669296d-1bdf-527a-aa02-77c5f5fc6df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380576} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2aaa4ba-aa2b-5c63-98dd-d56973b99ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "944155a1-9519-5409-8508-216f9904bbe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-109859" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 5$ matrix. What is the image of ${R}^{5}$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{5}$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} & {a}_{4} & {a}_{5} \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{5}\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{3} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{4}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{4} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{5}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{5} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{5}$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172028 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26871e46-51ca-5680-a064-bcee4ac984fd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Curve Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1907b7ac-361f-5a36-92c3-9ab8f1cba2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $1$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381106} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c6e34d-de43-5ad8-9958-84b5c204e126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A pair of intersecting lines" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381107} {:answer/id #uuid "3eadc2a7-33f9-518b-b997-cc899a831d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A circle of radius $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381108} {:answer/id #uuid "d43b8717-9c04-5178-8d01-d3b35a43962f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $1$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381109} {:answer/id #uuid "bd261e77-9409-5c92-9d2a-3ddcd21d645b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A parabola" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2c6e34d-de43-5ad8-9958-84b5c204e126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A pair of intersecting lines" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381107} :answer-field/id #uuid "36451658-9400-5ef6-a2e1-d9be723dfb92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5bc05156-589a-5065-b39a-74b3a0544d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140571" :question/problem "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,11{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+12{x}_{1}+16{x}_{2}=20.\n$$\n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)=11{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $20{y}_{2}^{2}-5{y}_{1}^{2}$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note the following:\n\n$$\nC:\\,\\underbrace{11{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}}_{Q(x)}+12{x}_{1}+16{x}_{2}=20\n$$\n\nLet's write the given change of variables explicitly:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{1}+\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{1}-\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe know that the given change of variables reduces $Q(x)$ to its canonical form. Therefore, performing the change of variables on $C,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+12{x}_{1}+16{x}_{2} & =20 \\\\ 20{y}_{2}^{2}-5{y}_{1}^{2}+12(\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{1}+\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{2})+16(\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{1}-\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{2}) & =20 \\\\ 20{y}_{2}^{2}-5{y}_{1}^{2}+20{y}_{1} & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we complete the square for the variable ${y}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{y}_{2}^{2}-5{y}_{1}^{2}+20{y}_{1} & =20 \\\\ 4{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1} & =4 \\\\ 4{y}_{2}^{2}-({y}_{1}^{2}-4{y}_{1}+4-4) & =4 \\\\ 4{y}_{2}^{2}-({y}_{1}-2)^{2}+4 & =4 \\\\ 4{y}_{2}^{2}-({y}_{1}-2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, performing the change of variables \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{z}_{1} &={y}_{1}-2, \\\\ {z}_{2} &={y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{2}^{2}-({y}_{1}-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4{z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents the pair of intersecting lines ${z}_{1}=2{z}_{2}$ and ${z}_{1}=-2{z}_{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443c2ac2-d73e-5209-b21f-beb333bf7d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨(A∧B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381370} {:answer/id #uuid "ea606823-2fa9-5cc2-990c-5045edd76dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381371} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7ab119-0282-5fbe-9bf9-0e338586bd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧(B∨A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381372} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3b63ed-53f9-5121-b506-5b94b2f06ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381373} {:answer/id #uuid "baa4f7d6-0324-5b7e-8071-793d1a8bec13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea606823-2fa9-5cc2-990c-5045edd76dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381371} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc686a5e-3a2b-5cc8-ad6d-1246bf1f5079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "694a195b-decb-5476-962c-92767f80b122" :question/math-academy-id "q-170735" :question/problem "$x$ is rational  **or** greater than $10.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is greater than $10$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is rational}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x>10}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4cb6d86-6aac-5d9a-a775-6b92f3e4ec46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧(B∨C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381377} {:answer/id #uuid "1c4ef4a3-535f-5532-a286-17ba44069aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∧C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381378} {:answer/id #uuid "1f750b80-7652-56ea-8e12-3af7c8f97f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨(B∧C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381379} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0e29d-19b6-5571-9682-b9f4dd89f92a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381380} {:answer/id #uuid "37903da6-d364-5436-9ac0-fbe2cbb768a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9de0e29d-19b6-5571-9682-b9f4dd89f92a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381380} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f97b5e3-e472-554b-a8b1-3aad913890b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "162c5a52-c662-54da-a9dc-018534c818f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-170748" :question/problem "$x$ is irrational **or** rational, **and** $x$ is positive.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is irrational\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is positive" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is irrational or rational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is irrational}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is rational }}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive. This corresponds to $C.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is irrational }\\text{ or }\\text{ rational }}_{A\\,∨\\,B}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is positive}}_{C},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∨B)∧C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9edf1556-11ca-5513-8e2a-c7d26ff5cf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381384} {:answer/id #uuid "57ed04a2-d471-5dbc-bc93-8957767cf212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381385} {:answer/id #uuid "4811b7b7-ccee-5ecf-9255-28175f022a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381386} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2b79e0-c6e8-5506-b6eb-014212d3f16b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381387} {:answer/id #uuid "509f6a97-4965-5f73-857c-a8b6f7a59c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9edf1556-11ca-5513-8e2a-c7d26ff5cf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381384} :answer-field/id #uuid "5efc1b68-b83f-54e2-8808-6f16fa2f13eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c69501f-1104-54ff-b9ef-9bcc718d509f" :question/math-academy-id "q-170756" :question/problem "$x$ is positive, **and** $x$ is irrational **or** integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is irrational\n\n- $R(x):$ $x$ is integer" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is positive. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is irrational or integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is irrational}}_{Q}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is integer}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is positive}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is irrational}\\text{ or integer}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧(Q∨R).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9929c09c-8f33-57ee-88cb-38daa710dcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453544} {:answer/id #uuid "1f16da6c-f534-5d72-880c-f328ccd0c191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f16da6c-f534-5d72-880c-f328ccd0c191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453545} :answer-field/id #uuid "9154c3d8-007c-5ee3-8a3b-e0dd67cef6cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8124e520-c402-5a54-9af8-c0ce7d475102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453546} {:answer/id #uuid "bce7b7f6-753e-5b37-b888-86bfae6f9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bce7b7f6-753e-5b37-b888-86bfae6f9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453547} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c84fe16-6e6b-5a98-b741-ab03c807812b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454523} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1a128bf-59d0-5ed3-9481-22081c32fcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453548} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fa2398-f7d9-5cc4-b8aa-f1a48a45fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1fa2398-f7d9-5cc4-b8aa-f1a48a45fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453549} :answer-field/id #uuid "f34b228d-dfef-5a02-826b-d0dc59fab7b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5934422-10d9-59ea-acc1-a33dbe6bcea0" :question/math-academy-id "q-171906" :question/problem "Let $m\\in N$ and $n\\in N.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∃\\,n\\in N,\\,5\\le n.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)$ is $N.$\n- **III.** $∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For every natural $m$ there exists natural $n$ such that $m\\le n.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true since $5\\le n$ for some natural number $n$ (e.g., for $n=6$).\n\n- Statement II is true. The predicate\n\n$$\nP(m):\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\n$$\n\nis true for any natural $m.$ For example,\n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\n$$\n\nis true since we can take $n=2.$ Similarly,\n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,2\\le n\n$$\n\nis true since we can take $n=3.$ And so on. In general, it's sufficient to take $n=m+1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀\\,m\\in N\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n}_{P(m)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(m)$ is true over the universal set $N.$ And, according to statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "791ba16d-0fde-5494-ae38-151cf6473679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381497} {:answer/id #uuid "570ac923-c70f-5b05-85ab-6d0e3179805a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381498} {:answer/id #uuid "26713a16-ca66-5149-b579-24b29515572c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381499} {:answer/id #uuid "814273a2-7641-537c-b209-0d0278585880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381500} {:answer/id #uuid "87001085-7898-5d47-97c2-c648e169d76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "814273a2-7641-537c-b209-0d0278585880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381500} :answer-field/id #uuid "56d3c014-7399-5320-a01a-ad25e78491d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8a305e0-7087-5ce5-b288-8389af590e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-175349" :question/problem "$x$ is a multiple of $3$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $3$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is a multiple of }3}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d99eb173-3abf-5775-a859-5a92ae2ae01f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∨(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381504} {:answer/id #uuid "df7b7424-fa58-5870-87bc-c682e2678be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∧(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381505} {:answer/id #uuid "28e544d4-09ee-5450-aac7-cedff79d4967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((N∨R)∧P)∨I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381506} {:answer/id #uuid "d99f5091-2095-5600-a488-bf4114dc1018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧R)∧(P∧I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381507} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd81fe8-96cc-5534-bfef-3c16765feb7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧R)∨(P∧I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df7b7424-fa58-5870-87bc-c682e2678be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∧(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381505} :answer-field/id #uuid "33ea1fa2-4f60-58ac-aee0-0a9d809fa209" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "357fd90c-bc44-5b21-9839-d55874391b78" :question/math-academy-id "q-175377" :question/problem "$x$ is negative **or** rational, **and** $x$ is positive **or** an  integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\n- $R(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $I(x):$ $x$ is an integer" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$,\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative **or** rational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is negative }}_{N}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is rational }}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive **or** an integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is positive }}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is an integer }}_{I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨I.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x\\text{ is negative or rational}}_{N\\,∨\\,R}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{x\\text{ is positive or an integer }}_{P\\,∨\\,I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∨R)∧(P∨I).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} {:answer/id #uuid "37313c70-39b7-5dc9-b3c4-a19acf370901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43f4f46-1ff7-5a5f-b67a-a7033ebb99e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ca0b4c-5971-598e-b066-6bedf819e07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe01474-e943-5480-b617-9630e94ff1a0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fce173-02a3-518a-95ef-ae472714bf66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f5bbf3-595e-55dd-8c22-bb49db12000e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44159662-1bf3-5bee-9ce6-75e394e9c1e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-183586" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$\n- **III.** $∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For all reals $x$ and $y,$ we have $\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $\\sqrt{2y}\\in R$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=-1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(x)$ is false for all values $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-1.$ Similarly,\n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-2.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $y=-x$ for any value of $x.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in R\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ is true over the universal set $R.$ But, according to statement II, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5b8712-0349-5ec9-be84-86313e9383f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453664} {:answer/id #uuid "99222c1c-3a4e-584c-88d0-dc8348b68220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f5b8712-0349-5ec9-be84-86313e9383f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453664} :answer-field/id #uuid "68de867c-02cd-57fa-bd09-3c999d6ea9c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311c0395-78e4-5af6-9ae4-5e9d6edf2fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453666} {:answer/id #uuid "532515bd-87e1-5e9b-b032-e51385cc6bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "532515bd-87e1-5e9b-b032-e51385cc6bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453667} :answer-field/id #uuid "5da7d4ee-3b45-5d05-bbd5-5970db34cb14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35033423-0e24-5eb3-ad49-542e49a2f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453668} {:answer/id #uuid "94aaeb7f-f626-58e9-8908-cbdc37a51c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35033423-0e24-5eb3-ad49-542e49a2f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453668} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e46de2-a550-5250-aeda-06a46b9a6b77" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42d7175e-7275-5d58-9cbb-adf651178f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183597" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Z$ and $y\\in Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x+1=0.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)$ is $∅.$\n- **III.** $∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a integer $y$ such that, for every integer $x,$ we have $x+y=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $x+1=0$ is not true for some integer $x.$ Say, for $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The predicate\n\n$$\nP(y):\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\n$$\n\nis false for every value of $y.$ For example,\n\n$$\nP(0):∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x=0\n$$\n\nis false for any $x\\ne 0.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $x\\ne -y$ for any $y\\in Z.$ Therefore, its truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement III is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,y\\in Z\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0}_{P(y)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(y)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement II, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f18e7d-fdb8-53fe-8f50-eaaac3ed1598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed5ac1a-9b04-5b9c-be9d-47fe1e8d63d8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} {:answer/id #uuid "443319b0-9a52-570e-9382-2ad4c166bcd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} :answer-field/id #uuid "e823795e-dd00-51ef-b876-a9f7aa0d9ea5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbba717-65e5-566d-8fd3-783fb2ce62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471291} {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292} :answer-field/id #uuid "a75d0c30-1919-56dd-97c7-3982426fe9c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "391922f6-f189-52a8-9bf4-83a4fbad32e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183598" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,2y=0.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$\n- **III.** $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a real $x$ such that, for every real $y,$ we have $xy=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $2y=0$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false.  The predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nis true for some $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,0\\cdot y=0\n$$\n\nis true. Therefore, its truth set is not empty.\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a7fb68-c72a-5e28-abef-c9c14c8731f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471305} {:answer/id #uuid "7d21b609-6f91-5663-ae33-506abb094118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d21b609-6f91-5663-ae33-506abb094118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471306} :answer-field/id #uuid "13da0634-93a4-522e-a9c5-ed03620db5cd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8b210b-083a-55dd-9b97-7d0ce1e26364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471307} {:answer/id #uuid "fd233510-4eb3-506c-8a37-8436954cbcf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8b210b-083a-55dd-9b97-7d0ce1e26364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471307} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b458786-6bfd-5503-9728-a374253066de" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fe7e95-dafd-55e3-a099-2e08519b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471309} {:answer/id #uuid "47e244b1-8fbd-5931-8cbe-a1843732e9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86fe7e95-dafd-55e3-a099-2e08519b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471309} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fddddbd-d644-5857-bcfb-d2ac64e0c2e6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e3ef236-7e81-55bf-8f08-564fa1c1ae50" :question/math-academy-id "q-183669" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}y=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,x{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}>3\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it is placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,xy=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,xz>3\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀$ that uses $z:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,xy=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀z\\in (1,2),\\,\\overbrace{x{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>3}^{\\text{scope of }∀z})\n$$\n\n \n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∃{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>3\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2883b9ba-32bd-5ff5-bcce-b579c830b5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471365} {:answer/id #uuid "555b55f4-34bd-5b0e-9e56-002b7921c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555b55f4-34bd-5b0e-9e56-002b7921c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471366} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba74c19-e05e-599b-bbd8-455461faedc0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07894ab-f2fd-5837-8dce-530c9db39f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471367} {:answer/id #uuid "8256ae5a-2145-576f-b24c-70fde43e43bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07894ab-f2fd-5837-8dce-530c9db39f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471367} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f394222-c342-5bf2-9565-301ff724543e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c293a14-efb0-5e66-bdb9-90ab3fd059d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471369} {:answer/id #uuid "6b596922-2fca-5d75-b70f-37831468c2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b596922-2fca-5d75-b70f-37831468c2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471370} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ad30a7-aa49-5946-bf6a-d22d986bc83e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d9a12d6-16ca-57db-975d-02505a889530" :question/math-academy-id "q-216618" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃z$ that uses $z:$ \n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>n+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,\\overbrace{{z}^{3}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}^{\\text{scope of }∃z}\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $y.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in N,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6732620-fad1-5dd3-98c5-07ba59d0b286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Factor in the SVD of a Rectangular Matrix: Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3deee69f-3a09-5221-985a-bd0ac7deae81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381944} {:answer/id #uuid "9063686e-f6d9-5985-ab01-efb95a0f5ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381945} {:answer/id #uuid "8b544ef9-20fe-5f86-891a-be7f8bae3513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381946} {:answer/id #uuid "6536ef14-8e86-50c8-955d-af6af6b6f266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b544ef9-20fe-5f86-891a-be7f8bae3513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381946} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9d9d60e-4182-57e9-b60d-64d8685d7b9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759