139807" :question/problem "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$10$** | **$28$** | **$13$** | **$34$** | **$40$** |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-8$ | $3$ | $10$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the plane $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$10$** | **$28$** | **$13$** | **$34$** | **$40$** |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-8$ | $3$ | $10$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 28 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 34 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 40\\end{bmatrix}}^{X}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}^{\\beta } & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}}^{y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eaee4e9-7be5-5c35-bc88-89697a15d75a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression That Passes Through the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ffa56ae-acb4-5f77-beef-bc7086a01f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #e